# GitHub draft publisher

[Script](../scripts/publish_draft.py). Push the current branch and create or
reuse its GitHub PR, then verify the head. Requires Python 3.11+, `git` and
authenticated `gh`.

## Run

Use only when [Opening a PR](../playbooks/opening-a-pr.md) selects the GitHub
CLI publication path. Resolve the installed script path and keep the project
repository as the working directory. Write the prepared PR body outside it.

```bash
python3 "{% if harness == "claude" %}{{ skill_root }}{% else %}<nstack-flow skill directory>{% endif %}/scripts/publish_draft.py" --base <base> --title "<title>" --body-file <body-file>
```

Use `--help` for the exact arguments. `--remote` selects the Git remote and
defaults to `origin`. It is not the separate Origin forge CLI. The script uses
the current `gh` repository and authentication context without switching them.

The checkout must be on a feature branch, have the selected remote and a known
base ref, and contain commits ahead of that base. Detached HEAD, the base
branch itself, unreadable/missing body input and unavailable authentication
are blockers. Existing uncommitted tracked edits remain uncommitted; they are
reported rather than silently included in a commit.

## Effects and result

The script pushes without force, reuses an existing open same-repository PR
for this branch, or creates a new draft. It verifies the open PR's head against
local HEAD. Existing non-draft PRs are not converted and can block publication.
An existing PR with a different base is reported, not silently retargeted.
It never marks ready, merges, enables auto-merge or watches CI.

Exit 0 returns JSON with `ok: true`, the URL, draft state, base, branch, head
SHA and whether tracked uncommitted edits remain. Exit 1 for a classified
publication failure returns `ok: false` with an error and repair.
CLI usage errors exit 2; unexpected process/decoding failures remain errors.

Head verification may repeat read-only PR queries while GitHub catches up.
It defaults to five attempts, two seconds apart, controlled by
`NSTACK_PUBLISH_ATTEMPTS` and `NSTACK_PUBLISH_RETRY_DELAY`. This is not a retry
of PR creation. A later failure can occur after the branch was pushed or a PR
created; inspect the reported state before rerunning and never claim delivery
without a verified result.

The helper does not authorize committing or publishing unreviewed work.
Opening a PR owns the publication gate, body format and built-in-tool
preference. A built-in tool failure does not authorize this fallback.
Afterward, remove only the caller's temporary body file and preserve evidence.
